          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Copy the following on a dot grid. For each figure draw two more lines to make a shape that has a line of symmetry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.218,
            0.172,
            0.832,
            0.297
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { c c c c } { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.22,
            0.31,
            0.86,
            0.442
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l l l l } { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } & { \\cdots } \\\\ \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.464,
            0.536,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.2 Rotational Symmetry"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.504,
            0.68,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The paper windmill in the picture looks symmetrical but there is no line of symmetry! However, if you fold "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{i}\\mathrm{t},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the two halves will not exactly overlap. On the other hand, if you rotate it by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " about the red point at the centre, the windmill looks exactly the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.698,
            0.501,
            0.885,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.698,
                0.501,
                0.885,
                0.64
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.641,
            0.679,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We say that the windmill has "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "rotational symmetry",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.686,
            0.886,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When talking of rotational symmetry, there is always a fixed point about which the object is rotated. This fixed point is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "centre of rotation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.755,
            0.885,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will the windmill above look exactly the same when rotated through an angle of less than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ } ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.801,
            0.247,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "No!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.823,
            0.888,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An angle through which a figure can be rotated to look exactly the same is called an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "angle of rotational symmetry",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", or just an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "angle of symmetry",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", for short."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 12,
